{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124169","id":4741587284,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGp7hVA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124169","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124169.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124169.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124169","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124169/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124169/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124169/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2a57bebd521c40f2f2819ebca72e3e1cb8a0bb6c","number":124169,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix reservation of array sizes in PrimitiveMesh classes","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nPR #105264 introduced calls to `.reserve()` which predict the amount of points and indices in the generated mesh. However, there are many mistakes in this PR, which lead to the reserved amount not quite matching.\r\n\r\nFor example, BoxMesh contains this code, which fails to consider `subdivide_d`:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nint num_points = (subdivide_h + 2) * (subdivide_w + 2) * 6;\r\n```\r\n\r\nCapsuleMesh, BoxMesh, PrismMesh, CylinderMesh, and TubeTrailMesh all had inaccurate reserve counts. CapsuleMesh was under-reserving, while the latter three were over-reserving.\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes the reserve code. The actual amount of points and indices is now correctly predicted for all shape types. The predictions now use constants to provide a readable semantic meaning to the intermediary steps.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs proof that this is correct, I added `DEV_ASSERT` checks in every function:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nDEV_ASSERT(points.size() == num_points);\r\nDEV_ASSERT(indices.size() == num_indices);\r\n```\r\n\r\nSince `DEV_ASSERT` only runs in dev mode builds, and since `.reserve()` is not behavior-critical, this PR should not affect the behavior of Godot projects, except for improved performance due to avoiding reallocations, or improved memory usage by allocating only what is needed.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlso, this PR:\r\n- Uses `const` more often in the changed lines (but does not use it absolutely everywhere it can be).\r\n- Uses `uint32_t` more often (`uint32_t` is required for the `==` in `DEV_ASSERT`)\r\n- Renames `onethird` to `one_third` and `twothirds` to `two_thirds` and makes them `constexpr`.\r\n- In `TubeTrailMesh::_create_mesh_array`, pre-calculates the scale values first, in order to determine `has_cap_top_mesh` and `has_cap_bottom_mesh`, in order to determine the point and index counts. This reduces indentation in `TubeTrailMesh::_create_mesh_array`, which is a lot of this PR's diffs.\r\n- Adds a comment `// The end edge vertex is duplicated to give it a different texture coordinate.` to explain why there is a seemingly duplicated end edge vertex.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nEvery line of C++ in this PR is fully human-written: designed by a human mind, and typed by human fingers. However, I used AI to generate GDScript tests, to check every combination of properties as a torture test.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com